 #language x-AMI "CbsCmnCpuCstC2Latency"
#string AMD_CBS_STR_ACPI_CST_C2_LATENCY_HELP                                    #language en-US    "Enter in microseconds (decimal value).\nLarger C2 latency values will reduce the number of C2 transitions and reduce C2 residency. Fewer transitions can help when performance is sensitive to the latency of C2 entry and exit. Higher residency can improve performance by allowing higher frequency boost and reduce idle core power. With Linux kernel 6.0 or later, the C2 transition cost is significantly reduced. The best value will be dependent on kernel version, use case, and workload."
