#string STR_PARITY_HELP                     #language eng  "A parity bit can be sent with the data bits to detect some transmission errors. Even: parity bit is 0 if the num of 1's in the data bits is even. Odd: parity bit is 0 if num of 1's in the data bits is odd.  Mark: parity bit is always 1. Space: Parity bit is always 0. Mark and Space Parity do not allow for error detection. They can be used as an additional data bit."

#string STR_ODD                             #language eng  "Odd"
#string STR_EVEN                            #language eng  "Even"
#string STR_MARK                            #language eng  "Mark"
#string STR_SPACE                           #language eng  "Space"

